<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Flemish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flanders is a historic region in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>, now largely in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. A wealthy centre of textile production and trade, it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s possessions in the Low Countries, where it was heavily affected by the wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flanders.jpg" alt="Flanders" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tom Lemmens · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Flanders.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
